name>Engel</surname><given-names>WK</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The histographic analysis of human muscle biopsies with regard to fiber types. 4. Children's biopsies</article-title><source>Neurology</source><year>1969</year><volume>19</volume><fpage>591</fpage><lpage>605</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">5814304</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B9"><label>9</label><element-citation publication-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Engel</surname><given-names>WK</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Goldensohn</surname><given-names>ES</given-names></name><name><surname>Appel</surname><given-names>SH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Central core disease and focal loss of crosss-triation</article-title><source>Scientific approaches to clinical neurology</source><year>1977</year><edition>1st ed</edition><publisher-loc>Philadelphia</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Lea &#x00026; Febiger</publisher-name><fpage>1555</fpage><lpage>1571</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="B10"><label>10</label><element-citation publication-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Engel</surname><given-names>WK</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Goldensohn</surname><given-names>ES</given-names></name><name><surname>Appel</surname><given-names>SH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Rod (nemaline) disease</article-title><source>Scientific approaches to clinical neurology</source><year>1977</year><edition>1st ed</edition><publisher-loc>Philadelphia</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Lea &#x00026; Febiger</publisher-name><fpage>1667</fpage><lpage>1691</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="B11"><label>11</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lambert</surname><given-names>CD</given-names></name></person-g