t"><label>Fig. 1</label><caption><p>The pathological findings of muscle biopsies for CFTD and CMT1P patients. Muscle biopsy shows type 1 fiber (dark fibers) predominance (&#x0003e; 55%) and relatively smaller (at least 12%) type 1 fibers compared to type 2 fibers (light fibers) (NADH-TR staining) (A). Muscle biopsy shows only type 1 fiber (dark fibers) predominance (&#x0003e; 55%) without other specific structural alterations. (NADH-TR staining) (B).</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="ymj-47-513-g001"/></fig><table-wrap id="T1" position="float"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p>Characteristics of 3 Patients with CFTD (No.1-3) and 6 Patients with CMT1P (No.4-9)</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="ymj-47-513-i001"/><table-wrap-foot><fn><p>D, delayed motor milestone; DD, delayed development; NL, normal; C, congenital hypotonia; L, lower extremity weakness; ND, not done; CFTD, congenital fiber type disproportion myopathy; CTFP, congenital myopathy with type 1 fiber predominance; TIFP, type 1 fiber predominance; RVH, right ventricular hypertrophy; T-ab, T-wave abnormality; NCV, nerve conduction velocity; EMG, electromyelography.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></floats-group></article>